---
import Slide from "@/components/slides/Slide.astro";

const notes =
    "asynchronous in a deadlock context:\n- a waiting task isn't blocking a thread, it's parked on the shelf\n- nobody is spinning: cpu idle, nothing errors, nothing is slow\n- a task waiting forever looks exactly like a task waiting normally\n- that's why async deadlocks are quiet instead of loud\n\nwhy it's hard to find:\n- threads: attach a debugger (gdb, lldb, a java thread dump), every stack is printed, the stuck ones name the line\n- async: you see idle workers waiting for work, and none of your code\n- the stuck task was packed into a value on the heap when it awaited; no thread runs it, so no stack shows it\n- optional live moment: attach lldb to the frozen demo, run \"bt all\", point out nothing of ours is there\n- go is a partial exception: goroutines keep their stacks, so a dump shows where they're stuck. the database half still hides\n\nthe turn:\n- the thing a task waits for can live somewhere else, so the loop can span two systems\n- in the next scenarios, part of the loop runs through the database. that's what makes them worth an autopsy";
---

<Slide
    kicker="why it's hard"
    title="a stuck task isn't on any stack."
    notes={notes}
>
    <div class="s-cols">
        <div class="s-card">
            <p class="s-card-label">a stuck thread</p>
            <div class="s-lines">
                <p>the debugger finds it parked on a lock</p>
                <p>its stack names the exact line</p>
                <p class="s-muted">five minutes, and you're done</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="s-card is-accent">
            <p class="s-card-label">a stuck task</p>
            <div class="s-lines">
                <p>every thread is idle, waiting for work</p>
                <p>none of your code is on any stack</p>
                <p class="s-muted">
                    the task is just data, waiting for a wake-up that never
                    comes
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-auto s-big">
        and often, half the loop isn't in your process at all.{" "}
        <span class="s-accent">it's in your database.</span>
    </p>
</Slide>
